In article <1993Feb28.043903.4408@spang.Camosun.BC.CA> ua123@freenet.Victoria.BC.CA (Matthew A. Skala) writes:
>
>In NH 3.1, I'm having trouble with sacrifices - I stand over the alter, do
>Meta-O for Offer, and get "nothing happens".  Yes, this is the correct
>alignment of altar.  I also tried just dropping the item to be sacrificed
>on the altar, with no result.  Is the problem that my corpses are not
>fresh enough?  If so, what can I do about it - I'm carrying them to the
>altar as fast as I can after killing them.

Yup, the corpses are stale. If you can't carry corpses to the altar
fast enough, you should kill them close to the altar. There are
several ways to do this:

1. Let the monster chase you to the altar.
2. Summon a monster near the altar (w/ scroll/wand of create monster,
   bag of tricks, cursed scroll of genocide...)
3. Zap the stale corpse with a Wand of Undead Turning, bringing it
   back to life; then kill it all over again, but near the altar.

Or use your imagination...
